      "content": "1. Cell – Definition and Discovery"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The cell is the fundamental structural and functional unit of all living organisms.",
        "Cell Theory was proposed by Matthias Schleiden and Theodor Schwann, and expanded by Rudolf Virchow ('Omnis cellula-e-cellula').",
        "Prokaryotic cells lack a membrane-bound nucleus and organelles, while Eukaryotic cells possess a well-defined nucleus.",
        "Mitochondria and Chloroplasts are semi-autonomous organelles containing their own DNA and ribosomes.",
        "Lysosomes contain hydrolytic digestive enzymes and are commonly known as the suicidal bags of the cell."
      ],
      "id": "gu4sjjn"
